SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 7:30 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 7:15 PM.\nOn stage: 8:10 PM–8:50 PM.\nACT II
  Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — p
 roduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time dan
 cers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Ti
 me.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgi
 ving and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are ca
 lled unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedu
 le\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mas
 ter: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-
 N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Seraphs ***\nAngels
  - Seraphs — Costume (you provide): Pink Seamless Tights\, Flesh-tone 
 camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Light Stage Makeup
 \; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provides): Gold Halo headp
 iece\nLight Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n• Powder matching skinton
 e\n• Light brown eye shadow applied to the crease with an eye shadow b
 rush\n• Dark Brown/Black eyeliner and black mascara. No fake lashes.\n
 • Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t loo
 k washed out in the stage lights)\n• Red or Dark Red lipstick\nDancers
  of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostu
 me Care Guidelines:\n• Handle costume pieces with care while changing 
 to prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly notify Ballet Arkans
 as in the event of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter 
 how significant\n• Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, 
 or hang costumes by their elastic straps\n• Refrain from sitting on th
 e floor while in costume\n• Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, o
 r launder any costume or accessory\n• Never apply stage make-up while 
 in costume and shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on
  costume during its removal\n• Refrain from the use of spray perfume o
 r cologne while in costume\n• Never wear any garment not assigned to c
 ast member\n• Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in costu
 me\, with the exception of water\n• Do not remove costumes from their 
 assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n• Remove all bobby pins u
 sed to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n• Return all h
 eadpieces to their assigned bags\n• Comply fully with any and all upda
 tes to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do not pack markers\, p
 aints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
